Alright, sorry to spam you all with the answer to my own problem, but we found the problem (or at least the fix) - fully deleting all the libraries relating to plyr, reshape2, ggplot2 etc and installing new versions in their place.  Still not clear why it only showed up for some users though it might have been a similar issue to this one https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/issues/727 and be dependent on the way we need to install libraries (not from R, which does not have access to the internet due to security restrictions).

PE

