I can think of several fancier ways to do this (including defining a formatter function), but here's a simple manual way that indicates the chromosome on the first bp within each batch.

Define these before the declaration of the graphing code:
bpBreaks <- as.character(c(10, 12, 14, 15, 2, 20, 6))
bpLabels <- c("1", "", "", "2", "", "3", "")

Add this to the graphing code:
scale_x_discrete(breaks=bpBreaks, labels=bpLabels) + xlab("Chromosome") +

